#### 1. Process Identity Retention Through Mutation
In [`_verified_toolhelp_children`](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/6bbf0095-0d8/gemini/library_mirror.py#L623-L673), each child process is pinned via native handle (`_open_ownership_handle`) immediately upon initial enumeration. The exact 100ns FILETIME creation stamp is checked against the parent's creation stamp (`native_created >= parent_native_created`), followed by dual parent/child liveness validations across a second snapshot. Mutations ([`_assign_owned_handle`](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/6bbf0095-0d8/gemini/library_mirror.py#L2401-L2412), [`_terminate_owned_handle`](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/6bbf0095-0d8/gemini/library_mirror.py#L2414-L2423), and [`_record_writer_identity`](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/6bbf0095-0d8/gemini/library_mirror.py#L2149-L2179)) operate directly on the acquired native handles from `_owned_handles`, preventing PID recycling and TOCTOU exploits.

#### 2. Handle Refcounting & Borrowed Popen Lifetimes
[`_CountedNativeHandle`](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/6bbf0095-0d8/gemini/library_mirror.py#L1570-L1636) synchronizes handle access with `self._guard`. Launcher handles are stored with `owns_close=False` and `owner=proc`, preventing garbage collection of `subprocess.Popen` while references remain borrowed. Crucially, dropping the borrowed owner (`del owner_to_drop`) executes outside `self._guard` (lines 1615, 1630), protecting against lock inversion or re-entrancy during `Popen.__del__`.

#### 3. Cancellation & Destination Exclusion Overlap
[`_discover_owned_children`](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/6bbf0095-0d8/gemini/library_mirror.py#L1712-L1788) reserves destination exclusion (`owner.reserve()`) and increments `_discovery_users`. Concurrent cancellation via [`terminate()`](file:///C:/Users/hello/AppData/Local/AgentControlRoom/worktrees/uoink-library/6bbf0095-0d8/gemini/library_mirror.py#L2439-L2454) marks `self._dead = True` and returns immediately without blocking. Proved children discovered during cancellation are registered into `_owned_handles`, and cleanup is deferred to the exit of `_discover_owned_children`, where `self.terminate()` terminates all proved children before dropping destination exclusion. The accepted `ff67b84` owner repair remains intact.

